# PR3 / workstream 4 — test baseline, by CAUSE

Owner: ws4a (`docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-25-ws4a-shipped-defects.md`).
Every later PR in the set (ws4b, ws4c, ws4d, ws4e) compares its full-suite result against this
file. Compare **causes**, never counts: a 13-to-13 count collision once hid a genuine new breakage
in this repo for seven consecutive tasks.

Command, in every measurement below:

    ~/.pyenv/versions/3.11.0/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -n auto -q

Collected count taken separately with `pytest tests/ --collect-only -q`.

Interpreter is the shared pyenv at `~/.pyenv/versions/3.11.0/bin/python`. The gitignored in-tree
`.venv` carries the PRE-PR2 stack and MUST NOT be used — two facts these plans depend on are false
in it.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
HOW TO USE THIS FILE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The gate is three clauses, all of which must hold:

  1. No NEW failure cause appears.
  2. The deploy-autoscaling cause is unchanged (same two tests, same two assertion strings).
  3. No test stopped existing. A falling collected count must be explained by an enumerated
     deletion, per ruling R1 ("irrelevant tests are DELETED, not migrated; name every deletion in
     its change description").

Clause 3 cannot be checked by a count alone, because N deletions plus N additions preserve it.
Check it the way ws4a did — diff the test trees against your base and confirm that no line
removing a `def test_`, an `async def test_`, or a `class Test` appears, and that no test file was
deleted. Both checks must come back empty unless a deletion is intended and named.

Never grep for a single quoted failure string to identify the deploy-autoscaling cause: its two
tests raise DIFFERENT messages, so matching one of them silently misses the other.

